[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2514590474","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99958#issuecomment-2514590474","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99958","id":2514590474,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V4ZsK","user":{"login":"jcostello","id":1168582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjg1ODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1168582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello","html_url":"https://github.com/jcostello","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T13:41:53Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T13:41:53Z","body":"Looks awesome. I notice that you can blend above the bounds of the probes. Is that correct? I tried and I got nice results but I wonder why above the bounds","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2514590474/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2514654222","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99958#issuecomment-2514654222","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99958","id":2514654222,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V4pQO","user":{"login":"lander-vr","id":31851431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUxNDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31851431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr","html_url":"https://github.com/lander-vr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T14:06:03Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T14:07:01Z","body":"> Looks awesome. I notice that you can blend above the bounds of the probes. Is that correct? I tried and I got nice results but I wonder why above the bounds\r\n\r\nI don't think limiting the property based on the size of the box really gives any UX improvements, if anything it could lead to unwanted changes of that value if the user accidentally makes the bounding box smaller than the max blending distance for those bounds. It would also feel needlessly restrictive, in my opinion. The actual blending is `min(reflections.data[ref_index].blend_distance, box_extents[i])`, so the blending itself is clamped based on the extents of the probe: even though you can drag the blend distance further, you shouldn't actually see a visual change if your probe is too small. You can however then increase the bounds of your probe and the internal bounding box will appear again keeping that blending distance. I think this feels a bit more flexible and nicer.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/25ae170e-4189-41c8-96d7-69969ff9c8c8","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2514654222/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2514997459","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99958#issuecomment-2514997459","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99958","id":2514997459,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V59DT","user":{"login":"jcostello","id":1168582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjg1ODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1168582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello","html_url":"https://github.com/jcostello","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T16:14:10Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T16:14:10Z","body":"> > Looks awesome. I notice that you can blend above the bounds of the probes. Is that correct? I tried and I got nice results but I wonder why above the bounds\r\n> \r\n> I don't think limiting the property based on the size of the box really gives any UX improvements, if anything it could lead to unwanted changes of that value if the user accidentally makes the bounding box smaller than the max blending distance for those bounds. It would also feel needlessly restrictive, in my opinion. The actual blending is `min(reflections.data[ref_index].blend_distance, box_extents[i])`, so the blending itself is clamped based on the extents of the probe: even though you can drag the blend distance further, you shouldn't actually see a visual change if your probe is too small. You can however then increase the bounds of your probe and the internal bounding box will appear again keeping that blending distance. I think this feels a bit more flexible and nicer.\r\n> \r\n\r\nThe only visual change I see using blender distance further is that you control how much of the sky blends. But maybe we can have a separate slider to control how much the sky blends when using `inside=false`","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2514997459/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515043716","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99958#issuecomment-2515043716","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99958","id":2515043716,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V6IWE","user":{"login":"lander-vr","id":31851431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUxNDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31851431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr","html_url":"https://github.com/lander-vr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T16:33:37Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T16:34:54Z","body":"> The only visual change I see using blender distance further is that you control how much of the sky blends. But maybe we can have a separate slider to control how much the sky blends when using inside=false\r\n\r\nI'm not entirely sure I understand what you mean. Is this not the behavior you would expect?\r\n![24_12_03_17_34__godot windows editor x86_64_NWy40nWQwd](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/12d99e62-27f3-4633-848d-a71287d855a3)\r\n\r\nKeep in mind that this PR is not really supposed to solve any of the current sky blending issues, this PR just deals with how things blend, not which things. To fix sky blending we need a priority system and sky visibility masks for reflection probes.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515043716/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515160715","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99958#issuecomment-2515160715","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99958","id":2515160715,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V6k6L","user":{"login":"lander-vr","id":31851431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUxNDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31851431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr","html_url":"https://github.com/lander-vr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T17:23:37Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T17:23:37Z","body":"> In Compatibility, I get a shader compilation error and the scene looks fully white. This doesn't occur in master.\r\n\r\nShould be fixed now! :)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515160715/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515235050","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99958#issuecomment-2515235050","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99958","id":2515235050,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V63Dq","user":{"login":"jcostello","id":1168582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjg1ODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1168582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello","html_url":"https://github.com/jcostello","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T17:55:32Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T17:55:32Z","body":"> I'm not entirely sure I understand what you mean. Is this not the behavior you would expect? !\r\n\r\nMaybe its the expected behavior but it feel strange to go beyond the limits of the probes. Like in my mind I dont know what it means to blend further that. Like I said, the only thing I notice was the sky.\r\n\r\nTo me, if the probe is only 1x1x1m, the maximum blend distance should be .5m. But I like better the unity approach that is with a float value from 0 to 1. Meaning 0 not blending at all and 1 the maximum distance from the center of the probe. Does it make sense in this case?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515235050/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515291905","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99958#issuecomment-2515291905","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99958","id":2515291905,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V7E8B","user":{"login":"lander-vr","id":31851431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUxNDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31851431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr","html_url":"https://github.com/lander-vr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T18:25:41Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T18:25:41Z","body":"> Maybe its the expected behavior but it feel strange to go beyond the limits of the probes.\r\n\r\nI'll add a bit more context in the tooltip.\r\n\r\n> Like I said, the only thing I notice was the sky.\r\n\r\nThis is strange, I cannot reproduce this. Once the blend distance reaches it's internal limit, there's no visual change for me when going far beyond that value. Looking at it pragmatically though, I don't think it matters too much. In normal use cases the blend range will only be a small part of the box.\r\n\r\n![24_12_03_19_10__godot windows editor x86_64_r8nNz5rVwF](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c69841f3-d60d-42e0-b6a0-e8ee23a1ee33)\r\n\r\n> To me, if the probe is only 1x1x1m, the maximum blend distance should be .5m. But I like better the unity approach that is with a float value from 0 to 1. Meaning 0 not blending at all and 1 the maximum distance from the center of the probe. Does it make sense in this case?\r\n\r\nI think this is mostly a case of getting used to this behavior if you're unfamiliar with it. In the end they're not vastly different.\r\nA % value of the bounds is more abstract in my opinion (For example % of which side?), and causes varying blend distances with different sizes probes.\r\nTo me a distance makes more sense, it's more predictable. A meter is a meter, regardless the size of the probe. The probe can have dimensions of 500m x 10m x 10m, but when the blend distance is set to 1 meter, it will still be 1 meter of equal blend on all sides.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515291905/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2521624038","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99958#issuecomment-2521624038","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99958","id":2521624038,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WTO3m","user":{"login":"lander-vr","id":31851431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUxNDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31851431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr","html_url":"https://github.com/lander-vr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-05T22:39:36Z","updated_at":"2024-12-05T22:39:36Z","body":"Rebased to resolve conflict. :)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2521624038/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2540144177","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99958#issuecomment-2540144177","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99958","id":2540144177,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XZ4Yx","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-12T22:33:55Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T22:33:55Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2540144177/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":3,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]